        <body>
            <div xml:id="d464">

                <pb facs="0619" n="305" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg305"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/87</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at London</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate General</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                        notAfter="1914-08-18T13:15:00-05:00" notBefore="1914-08-18T00:00:00+00:00"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">undated</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Received <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1914-08-18T13:15:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 18, 1914, 1:15 p.m.</hi>
                        </date></hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Marshal of prize court informs me neutrals can obtain possession of their
                    property not contraband by applying procurator general, Treasury Chambers,
                    Whitehall, who will require proof ownership and particulars as to freight
                    whether paid or unpaid.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
